--- driving --headless ---
Error: --headless is not a /foundry:start flag

   --no-ui declares that this run has no browsable UI, so the SIGHT
   browser audit is not part of it. That is what --headless silently
   did here, and it is not what --headless means anywhere else.

   --headless and --headed choose the BROWSER MODE the SIGHT stream
   drives. The sight skill documents where those are set, and it is
   never this command line.
exit=1
--- driving --no-ui: still one meaning, still threaded ---
FOUNDRY_NO_UI=true
